<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  {% assign title = "What's my local AI?" %}
  {% include 'head' %}
  <body x-data="app()">
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">skip to content</a>

    {% include 'header' %}

    <main id="main">
      <nav class="scrollspy" aria-label="on this page" x-cloak>
        <template x-for="item in spyItems" :key="item.id">
          <button
            type="button"
            class="scrollspy-dot"
            :class="{ active: activeSection === item.id }"
            :aria-label="item.label"
            :aria-current="activeSection === item.id ? 'true' : null"
            @click="scrollToSection(item.id)"
          >
            <span class="scrollspy-label" x-text="item.label"></span>
          </button>
        </template>
      </nav>

      <div class="hero">
        <h1 class="hero-title">What's my local AI?</h1>
        <p class="hero-sub">Check what's the best model you can run locally!</p>
        <noscript>
          <p class="noscript-note">
            This tool needs JavaScript. The detection runs locally in your browser, so there's nothing to upload.
          </p>
        </noscript>
      </div>

      <section id="detect-panel" class="machine">
        <div class="machine-head">
          <h2 class="section-heading ds-text-gradient ds-text-gradient--animated">Your machine</h2>
          <button type="button" class="reset-specs" x-show="manual" x-cloak @click="resetSpecs">reset my specs</button>
        </div>
        <p class="specs-intro">
          We auto-detect what we can from your browser; everything else is a best guess. Tweak any value below to see
          what else could run.
        </p>

        <div class="machine-groups">
          <div class="spec-group">
            <h3 class="spec-group-title">Hardware</h3>
            <div class="spec-row spec-row--gpu">
              <div class="machine-spec" :class="{ custom: probeDone.gpu && !gpuDetected }">
                <div x-show="!probeDone.gpu" class="probe-overlay"><span class="probe-spinner"></span></div>
                <div :class="{ 'is-probing': !probeDone.gpu }" class="machine-spec-inner machine-spec-inner--gpu">
                  <div class="machine-spec-head">
                    <svg
                      class="spec-icon"
                      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                      fill="none"
                      stroke="currentColor"
                      stroke-width="1.5"
                      stroke-linecap="round"
                      stroke-linejoin="round"
                    >
                      <rect x="6" y="6" width="12" height="12" rx="2"/><rect x="9" y="9" width="6" height="6" rx="1"/><path d="M6 10H4"/><path d="M6 14H4"/><path d="M20 10H18"/><path d="M20 14H18"/><path d="M10 6V4"/><path d="M14 6V4"/><path d="M10 20V18"/><path d="M14 20V18"/>
                    </svg>
                    <span class="machine-spec-label">GPU</span>
                    <span class="spec-edit-tag" x-show="probeDone.gpu && !gpuDetected" x-cloak>edited</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class="spec-select-wrap">
                    <select
                      class="spec-select"
                      aria-label="GPU"
                      :disabled="!probeDone.gpu"
                      @change="setGpu($event.target.value)"
                    >
                      <template x-for="group in gpuOptionGroups" :key="group.label">
                        <optgroup :label="group.label">
                          <template x-for="opt in group.options" :key="opt.value">
                            <option
                              :value="opt.value"
                              :disabled="!!opt.disabled"
                              :selected="gpuSel === opt.value"
                              x-text="opt.label"
                            ></option>
                          </template>
                        </optgroup>
                      </template>
                    </select>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="spec-group">
            <h3 class="spec-group-title">Memory</h3>
            <div class="spec-row spec-row--2">
              <div class="machine-spec" :class="{ custom: probeDone.ram && !ramDetected }">
                <div x-show="!probeDone.ram" class="probe-overlay"><span class="probe-spinner"></span></div>
                <div :class="{ 'is-probing': !probeDone.ram }" class="machine-spec-inner">
                  <div class="machine-spec-head">
                    <svg
                      class="spec-icon"
                      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                      fill="none"
                      stroke="currentColor"
                      stroke-width="1.5"
                      stroke-linecap="round"
                      stroke-linejoin="round"
                    >
                      <rect x="4" y="4" width="16" height="16" rx="2"/><path d="M8 4v2a1 1 0 0 0 1 1h6a1 1 0 0 0 1-1V4"/><path d="M8 16v1a1 1 0 0 0 1 1h6a1 1 0 0 0 1-1v-1"/><path d="M8 12h8"/>
                    </svg>
                    <span class="machine-spec-label">RAM</span>
                    <span class="spec-edit-tag" x-show="probeDone.ram && !ramDetected" x-cloak>edited</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class="spec-stepper">
                    <button
                      type="button"
                      aria-label="decrease RAM"
                      @pointerdown="startRepeat(() => adjust('ram', -1))"
                      @pointerup="stopRepeat()"
                      @pointerleave="stopRepeat()"
                      @pointercancel="stopRepeat()"
                      @keydown.enter.prevent="adjust('ram', -1)"
                      @keydown.space.prevent="adjust('ram', -1)"
                    >
                      −
                    </button>
                    <span class="spec-stepper-value" x-text="probeDone.ram ? ramValue() : '-- GB'"></span>
                    <button
                      type="button"
                      aria-label="increase RAM"
                      @pointerdown="startRepeat(() => adjust('ram', 1))"
                      @pointerup="stopRepeat()"
                      @pointerleave="stopRepeat()"
                      @pointercancel="stopRepeat()"
                      @keydown.enter.prevent="adjust('ram', 1)"
                      @keydown.space.prevent="adjust('ram', 1)"
                    >
                      +
                    </button>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="machine-spec" :class="{ custom: probeDone.vram && !vramDetected }">
                <div x-show="!probeDone.vram" class="probe-overlay"><span class="probe-spinner"></span></div>
                <div :class="{ 'is-probing': !probeDone.vram }" class="machine-spec-inner">
                  <div class="machine-spec-head">
                    <svg
                      class="spec-icon"
                      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                      fill="none"
                      stroke="currentColor"
                      stroke-width="1.5"
                      stroke-linecap="round"
                      stroke-linejoin="round"
                    >
                      <rect x="6" y="6" width="12" height="12" rx="2"/><rect x="9" y="9" width="6" height="6" rx="1"/><path d="M6 10H4"/><path d="M6 14H4"/><path d="M20 10H18"/><path d="M20 14H18"/><path d="M10 6V4"/><path d="M14 6V4"/><path d="M10 20V18"/><path d="M14 20V18"/>
                    </svg>
                    <span class="machine-spec-label">VRAM</span>
                    <span class="spec-edit-tag" x-show="probeDone.vram && !vramDetected" x-cloak>edited</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class="spec-stepper">
                    <button
                      type="button"
                      aria-label="decrease VRAM"
                      @pointerdown="startRepeat(() => adjust('vram', -1))"
                      @pointerup="stopRepeat()"
                      @pointerleave="stopRepeat()"
                      @pointercancel="stopRepeat()"
                      @keydown.enter.prevent="adjust('vram', -1)"
                      @keydown.space.prevent="adjust('vram', -1)"
                    >
                      −
                    </button>
                    <span class="spec-stepper-value" x-text="probeDone.vram ? vram + ' GB' : '-- GB'"></span>
                    <button
                      type="button"
                      aria-label="increase VRAM"
                      @pointerdown="startRepeat(() => adjust('vram', 1))"
                      @pointerup="stopRepeat()"
                      @pointerleave="stopRepeat()"
                      @pointercancel="stopRepeat()"
                      @keydown.enter.prevent="adjust('vram', 1)"
                      @keydown.space.prevent="adjust('vram', 1)"
                    >
                      +
                    </button>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="spec-group">
            <h3 class="spec-group-title">Platform</h3>
            <div class="spec-row spec-row--3">
              <div class="machine-spec" :class="{ custom: probeDone.cpu && !coresDetected }">
                <div x-show="!probeDone.cpu" class="probe-overlay"><span class="probe-spinner"></span></div>
                <div :class="{ 'is-probing': !probeDone.cpu }" class="machine-spec-inner">
                  <div class="machine-spec-head">
                    <svg
                      class="spec-icon"
                      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                      fill="none"
                      stroke="currentColor"
                      stroke-width="1.5"
                      stroke-linecap="round"
                      stroke-linejoin="round"
                    >
                      <rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="1.5"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/><path d="M7 10H4"/><path d="M7 14H4"/><path d="M20 10H17"/><path d="M20 14H17"/><path d="M10 7V4"/><path d="M14 7V4"/><path d="M10 20V17"/><path d="M14 20V17"/>
                    </svg>
                    <span class="machine-spec-label">CPU</span>
                    <span class="spec-edit-tag" x-show="probeDone.cpu && !coresDetected" x-cloak>edited</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class="spec-stepper">
                    <button
                      type="button"
                      aria-label="decrease CPU cores"
                      @pointerdown="startRepeat(() => adjustCores(-1))"
                      @pointerup="stopRepeat()"
                      @pointerleave="stopRepeat()"
                      @pointercancel="stopRepeat()"
                      @keydown.enter.prevent="adjustCores(-1)"
                      @keydown.space.prevent="adjustCores(-1)"
                    >
                      −
                    </button>
                    <span class="spec-stepper-value" x-text="probeDone.cpu ? (cores || '--') + ' cores' : '--'"></span>
                    <button
                      type="button"
                      aria-label="increase CPU cores"
                      @pointerdown="startRepeat(() => adjustCores(1))"
                      @pointerup="stopRepeat()"
                      @pointerleave="stopRepeat()"
                      @pointercancel="stopRepeat()"
                      @keydown.enter.prevent="adjustCores(1)"
                      @keydown.space.prevent="adjustCores(1)"
                    >
                      +
                    </button>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="machine-spec" :class="{ custom: probeDone.os && !osDetected }">
                <div x-show="!probeDone.os" class="probe-overlay"><span class="probe-spinner"></span></div>
                <div :class="{ 'is-probing': !probeDone.os }" class="machine-spec-inner">
                  <div class="machine-spec-head">
                    <svg
                      class="spec-icon"
                      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                      fill="none"
                      stroke="currentColor"
                      stroke-width="1.5"
                      stroke-linecap="round"
                      stroke-linejoin="round"
                    >
                      <rect x="2" y="4" width="20" height="14" rx="2"/><path d="M8 22H16"/><path d="M12 18V22"/><path d="M6 9L8.5 11L6 13"/>
                    </svg>
                    <span class="machine-spec-label">OS</span>
                    <span class="spec-edit-tag" x-show="probeDone.os && !osDetected" x-cloak>edited</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class="spec-select-wrap">
                    <select
                      class="spec-select"
                      aria-label="OS"
                      :disabled="!probeDone.os"
                      @change="setOS($event.target.value)"
                    >
                      <template x-for="opt in osOptions" :key="opt.value">
                        <option :value="opt.value" :selected="osSel === opt.value" x-text="opt.label"></option>
                      </template>
                    </select>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="machine-spec machine-spec--webgpu" :class="{ custom: probeDone.webgpu && !webgpuDetected }">
                <div x-show="!probeDone.webgpu" class="probe-overlay"><span class="probe-spinner"></span></div>
                <div :class="{ 'is-probing': !probeDone.webgpu }" class="machine-spec-inner">
                  <div class="machine-spec-head">
                    <svg
                      class="spec-icon"
                      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                      fill="none"
                      stroke="currentColor"
                      stroke-width="1.5"
                      stroke-linecap="round"
                      stroke-linejoin="round"
                    >
                      <polygon points="13,2 4,14 12,14 11,22 20,10 12,10"/>
                    </svg>
                    <span class="machine-spec-label">WebGPU</span>
                    <span class="spec-edit-tag" x-show="probeDone.webgpu && !webgpuDetected" x-cloak>edited</span>
                  </div>
                  <button
                    type="button"
                    class="spec-switch"
                    :class="{ on: webgpu }"
                    role="switch"
                    :aria-checked="webgpu"
                    :aria-label="webgpu ? 'WebGPU supported — click to disable' : 'WebGPU not available — click to enable'"
                    @click="toggleWebGPU()"
                  >
                    <span class="spec-switch-knob"></span>
                  </button>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <script id="model-data" type="application/json">
        {{ models | json }}
      </script>
      <script id="gpu-database" type="application/json">
        {{ gpu_database | json }}
      </script>
      <script id="apple-chips" type="application/json">
        {{ apple_chips | json }}
      </script>

      <section class="best-pick-row" id="best-pick-row">
        <h2 class="section-heading ds-text-gradient ds-text-gradient--animated">Your local model</h2>
        <p class="specs-intro" x-text="runnerHint"></p>

        <p class="mlx-note" x-show="vendor === 'apple'" x-cloak>
          <strong>Apple Silicon:</strong>
          <span x-show="runner === 'lmstudio'">
            LM Studio also runs MLX models. Filter the catalog with <code>lms get --mlx</code>.
          </span>
          <span x-show="runner === 'ollama'">
            Ollama also runs MLX models. Look for tags ending in <code>-mlx</code>.
          </span>
          The commands on this page use GGUF via llama.cpp and Metal.
        </p>

        <div class="best-pick-controls">
          <div class="tradeoff" role="group" aria-label="choose a performance vs. resource trade-off">
            <span class="tradeoff-end">lean</span>
            <input
              id="perf-slider"
              class="tradeoff-range"
              type="range"
              aria-label="performance: lean vs max performance"
              min="0"
              max="100"
              step="1"
              :value="Math.round(perfBias * 100)"
              @input="setPerfBias($event.target.value / 100)"
            >
            <span class="tradeoff-end">max performance</span>
          </div>
          <div class="runner-toggle" role="group" aria-label="choose how to run models">
            <button type="button" @click="setRunner('lmstudio')" :aria-pressed="runner === 'lmstudio'">
              LM Studio
            </button>
            <button type="button" @click="setRunner('ollama')" :aria-pressed="runner === 'ollama'">Ollama</button>
          </div>
          <button
            type="button"
            class="share-btn"
            @click="shareResult()"
            :class="{ copied: shareCopied }"
            aria-label="share your result"
          >
            <svg
              class="share-btn-icon"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              stroke-width="1.5"
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
            >
              <path d="M4 12v7a1 1 0 0 0 1 1h14a1 1 0 0 0 1-1v-7"/>
              <path d="M16 6l-4-4-4 4"/>
              <path d="M12 2v13"/>
            </svg>
            <span class="share-btn-label" x-text="shareCopied ? 'link copied!' : 'share'"></span>
          </button>
        </div>

        <article class="model-card best-pick-card" :class="{ tight: bestModel ? isTight(bestModel) : false }">
          <div x-show="!displayReady" class="probe-overlay"><span class="probe-spinner"></span></div>

          <template x-if="displayReady && bestModel">
            <div class="best-pick-body">
              <h3 class="model-name" x-text="bestModel.model_name"></h3>
              <button
                type="button"
                class="run-cmd"
                @click="copyCmd(bestModel)"
                :class="{ copied: copiedId === bestModel.id }"
                :aria-label="'copy command: ' + runCmd(bestModel)"
              >
                <code x-text="runCmd(bestModel)"></code>
                <span class="run-cmd-hint" x-text="copiedId === bestModel.id ? 'copied!' : 'copy'"></span>
              </button>
              <p class="model-blurb" x-show="bestModel.blurb" x-text="bestModel.blurb"></p>
              <div class="model-meta">
                <span class="chip" x-text="bestModel.parameters"></span>
                <span class="chip" x-text="'~' + bestModel.vram_requirements_gb + ' GB Q4'"></span>
                <template x-for="cap in bestModel.capabilities" :key="cap">
                  <span class="chip" x-text="cap"></span>
                </template>
                <span class="chip chip-tight" x-show="isTight(bestModel)">tight fit</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </template>

          <template x-if="displayReady && !bestModel">
            <div class="best-pick-body">
              <h3 class="model-name" x-text="'nothing fits in ' + vram + ' GB'"></h3>
              <p class="best-pick-why" x-show="closestBeyond.length > 0">The closest options:</p>
              <ul class="beyond-list" x-show="closestBeyond.length > 0">
                <template x-for="model in closestBeyond" :key="model.id">
                  <li>
                    <span class="beyond-list-name" x-text="model.model_name"></span>
                    <span class="beyond-list-gap" x-text="'~' + formatGap(model) + ' GB short'"></span>
                  </li>
                </template>
              </ul>
              <p class="best-pick-why">Tweak your specs above to see what changes.</p>
            </div>
          </template>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section class="models" id="models" :class="{ preview: !displayReady }">
        <h2 class="section-heading ds-text-gradient ds-text-gradient--animated">Other options</h2>
        <p class="ds-sr-only" role="status" aria-live="polite" x-effect="announceResults()" x-text="announcement"></p>

        <div class="options-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="model options">
          <button
            type="button"
            role="tab"
            id="tab-fits"
            class="options-tab"
            :class="{ active: effectiveTab === 'fits' }"
            :aria-selected="effectiveTab === 'fits'"
            :aria-label="'Fits, ' + alsoRuns.length + ' more models'"
            aria-controls="panel-fits"
            :tabindex="effectiveTab === 'fits' ? 0 : -1"
            @click="setTab('fits')"
            @keydown.arrow-right.prevent="setTab('beyond', true)"
            @keydown.arrow-left.prevent="setTab('beyond', true)"
            @keydown.home.prevent="setTab('fits', true)"
            @keydown.end.prevent="setTab('beyond', true)"
          >
            <span x-text="'Fits (' + alsoRuns.length + ')'"></span>
          </button>
          <button
            type="button"
            role="tab"
            id="tab-beyond"
            class="options-tab"
            x-show="beyondModels.length > 0"
            :class="{ active: effectiveTab === 'beyond' }"
            :aria-selected="effectiveTab === 'beyond'"
            :aria-label="'Out of reach, ' + beyondModels.length + ' models'"
            aria-controls="panel-beyond"
            :tabindex="effectiveTab === 'beyond' ? 0 : -1"
            @click="setTab('beyond')"
            @keydown.arrow-right.prevent="setTab('fits', true)"
            @keydown.arrow-left.prevent="setTab('fits', true)"
            @keydown.home.prevent="setTab('fits', true)"
            @keydown.end.prevent="setTab('beyond', true)"
          >
            <span x-text="'Out of reach (' + beyondModels.length + ')'"></span>
          </button>
        </div>

        <div id="panel-fits" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-fits" x-show="effectiveTab === 'fits'" tabindex="0">
          <div class="models-toolbar" x-show="alsoRuns.length > 0" x-cloak>
            <input
              type="search"
              class="model-search"
              placeholder="search name, capability…"
              aria-label="search models"
              x-model="filterQ"
            >
            <div class="filter-chips" role="group" aria-label="filter by capability">
              <template x-for="cap in availableCaps" :key="cap">
                <button
                  type="button"
                  class="filter-chip"
                  @click="toggleCap(cap)"
                  :class="{ active: filterCaps.includes(cap) }"
                  :aria-pressed="filterCaps.includes(cap)"
                  x-text="cap"
                ></button>
              </template>
            </div>
            <select class="model-sort" aria-label="sort models" x-model="filterSort">
              <option value="size-desc">largest first</option>
              <option value="size-asc">smallest first</option>
              <option value="name">name a–z</option>
            </select>
          </div>

          <template x-if="alsoRuns.length === 0">
            <p
              class="hint"
              x-text="bestModel ? 'nothing smaller on the list — your pick above is the sweet spot.' : 'no other models fit in ' + vram + ' GB.'"
            ></p>
          </template>

          <template x-if="alsoRuns.length > 0 && visibleAlsoRuns.length === 0">
            <p class="hint">nothing matches — try clearing the search or filters.</p>
          </template>

          <template x-if="visibleAlsoRuns.length > 0">
            <div>
              <div class="model-grid" id="fits-grid">
                <template x-for="model in shownAlsoRuns" :key="model.id">
                  <article class="model-card" :class="{ tight: isTight(model) }">
                    <h3 class="model-name" x-text="model.model_name"></h3>
                    <button
                      type="button"
                      class="run-cmd"
                      @click="copyCmd(model)"
                      :class="{ copied: copiedId === model.id }"
                      :aria-label="'copy command: ' + runCmd(model)"
                    >
                      <code x-text="runCmd(model)"></code>
                      <span class="run-cmd-hint" x-text="copiedId === model.id ? 'copied!' : 'copy'"></span>
                    </button>
                    <p class="model-blurb" x-show="model.blurb" x-text="model.blurb"></p>
                    <div class="model-meta">
                      <span class="chip" x-text="model.parameters"></span>
                      <span class="chip" x-text="'~' + model.vram_requirements_gb + ' GB Q4'"></span>
                      <template x-for="cap in model.capabilities" :key="cap">
                        <span class="chip" x-text="cap"></span>
                      </template>
                      <span class="chip chip-tight" x-show="isTight(model)">tight fit</span>
                    </div>
                  </article>
                </template>
              </div>
              <button
                type="button"
                class="show-all-toggle"
                x-show="alsoRuns.length > 3"
                @click="toggleShowAll"
                :aria-expanded="showAll"
                aria-controls="fits-grid"
                x-text="showAll ? 'show top 3' : 'show all ' + alsoRuns.length + ' models'"
              ></button>
            </div>
          </template>
        </div>

        <div
          id="panel-beyond"
          role="tabpanel"
          aria-labelledby="tab-beyond"
          x-show="effectiveTab === 'beyond'"
          tabindex="0"
        >
          <h3 class="beyond-title">How far off you are</h3>
          <p class="beyond-intro">
            These models need more memory than you have. The gap is the extra VRAM they want, at Q4.
          </p>
          <ul class="beyond-rows" id="beyond-rows" role="list">
            <template x-for="model in visibleBeyond" :key="model.id">
              <li class="beyond-row">
                <span class="beyond-row-name" x-text="model.model_name"></span>
                <span
                  class="beyond-row-specs"
                  x-text="model.parameters + ' · ~' + model.vram_requirements_gb + ' GB Q4'"
                ></span>
                <span class="beyond-row-gap" x-text="'~' + formatGap(model) + ' GB short'"></span>
              </li>
            </template>
          </ul>
          <button
            type="button"
            class="show-all-toggle"
            x-show="beyondModels.length > 6"
            @click="toggleBeyond"
            :aria-expanded="showBeyond"
            aria-controls="beyond-rows"
            x-text="showBeyond ? 'show fewer' : 'show all ' + beyondModels.length + ' models'"
          ></button>
        </div>

        <p class="catalog-note">
          Model data: models.dev snapshot {{ models.sources.models_dev }}, model registry {{ models.sources.registry }}.
          Sizes are Q4, refreshed weekly from the upstream catalogs.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="use-cases" id="use-cases">
        <h2 class="section-heading ds-text-gradient ds-text-gradient--animated">What can you do with it?</h2>
        <p class="specs-intro">
          Local models are private by design — everything stays on your machine. A few things people actually do:
        </p>
        <div class="use-case-grid">
          <article class="use-case">
            <h3 class="use-case-title">Private drafting</h3>
            <p class="use-case-body">
              Brainstorm, rewrite, or translate text with no data ever leaving your laptop. Perfect for work that isn't
              yours to share.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="use-case">
            <h3 class="use-case-title">Offline code help</h3>
            <p class="use-case-body">
              Autocomplete, explain a gnarly snippet, or write a quick script — even on a plane or in a dead zone.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="use-case">
            <h3 class="use-case-title">Read your own files</h3>
            <p class="use-case-body">
              Summarize that 50-page report, pull the action items from a meeting transcript, or chat with your notes —
              without uploading them anywhere.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="use-case">
            <h3 class="use-case-title">Zero-cost experiments</h3>
            <p class="use-case-body">
              Try open-weight models (reasoning, vision, tool calls) on your own hardware before paying for an API — the
              model list on this page is your playground.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="use-case">
            <h3 class="use-case-title">No throttle, no quota</h3>
            <p class="use-case-body">
              Run as much as you want. No rate limits, no token metering, no monthly bill — just your electricity.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="use-case">
            <h3 class="use-case-title">Learning &amp; tinkering</h3>
            <p class="use-case-body">
              The fastest way to build a mental model of what different model sizes are good at — swap models and feel
              the difference.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="detection-credit" id="detection-credit">
        <h2 class="section-heading ds-text-gradient ds-text-gradient--animated">How detection works</h2>
        <dl class="detection-credit-list">
          <div class="detection-credit-item">
            <dt>GPU</dt>
            <dd>WebGL renderer string</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="detection-credit-item">
            <dt>VRAM</dt>
            <dd>GPU database lookup, unified memory on Apple, or estimate from RAM</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="detection-credit-item">
            <dt>RAM</dt>
            <dd><code>navigator.deviceMemory</code>, cross-checked against the detected chip on Apple Silicon</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="detection-credit-item">
            <dt>CPU</dt>
            <dd><code>navigator.hardwareConcurrency</code></dd>
          </div>
          <div class="detection-credit-item">
            <dt>OS</dt>
            <dd>user agent parsing</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="detection-credit-item">
            <dt>WebGPU</dt>
            <dd><code>navigator.gpu</code> presence</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </section>
    </main>

